# Helm canonical deployment manifest — deterministic, forward-only.
# Columns:  <scope> <path-relative-to-repo-root>
#   base    = prod-faithful snapshot schema; applied ONLY on a FRESH database.
#   forward = forward-only hardening migration; applied once, idempotent.
# Run with scripts/db-migrate.sh (--plan | --apply | --verify).
# The ledger (public.helm_schema_migrations) makes re-runs idempotent and catches
# drift. This manifest is the ONLY sanctioned apply order; the deprecated
# full-schema/complete-setup.sql and ad-hoc phase files are intentionally absent.

# ---- BASE (fresh install only) --------------------------------------------
# Prod-extracted schema (2026-09-25). On an existing prod/staging DB this is
# skipped; the forward migrations below bring it to the hardened target state.
base     supabase/canonical-base/base-v1-2026-09-25.sql

# ---- FORWARD hardening (always, idempotent, in order) ---------------------
forward  supabase/migrations/0001_pricing_authority.sql
forward  supabase/migrations/0002_create_helm_user_lockdown.sql
forward  supabase/migrations/0003_money_integrity.sql
forward  supabase/migrations/0004_tenant_integrity.sql
forward  supabase/migrations/0005_least_privilege.sql
forward  supabase/migrations/0006_rls_access_gates.sql
forward  supabase/migrations/0007_rpc_authz_guards.sql
